  "details": "This was talked about a bit in #udon-questions\nRather than exposing a Player Transform directly (which can lead to security issues)\nI purpose a wrapped class that stores the reference to the Transform (but doesn't expose it) and only exposes the non-destructive parts of Transform to the end user.\nEssentially TrackingData except extended to allow for more than just Head and Hands and allows usage of methods such as TransformPoint, InverseTransformPoint, TransformDirection, etc.\nWrapper methods within the wrapped class could be restricted for security purposes and developers could use Transform methods in a secure manner right off the wrapped class instance.\nThe main difference between this and what Udon does now is being able to access methods that are otherwise not exposed and the VRChat developers still being able to maintain security over those exposed methods.\nFor example lets call our wrapped class WrappedTransform.\nThe instance of WrappedTransform wouldn't be passible to Object.Destroy but a world developer could still use something like WrappedTransform.InverseTransformPoint if they wanted.",
